  "boundedQuestion": "When a successor artifact names or retains an earlier revision, what proves that the exact parent was eligible to seed the successor rather than merely available and hashable?",
  "currentBestViewComparison": {
    "covered": [
      "EPHEMERAL-PUBLIC-PARENT-NOT-REPLAYABLE-001 requires immutable parent identity and replayability.",
      "REJECTED-DESCENDANT-QUARANTINE-001 prevents rejected ancestry or copied rejected content from silently returning."
    ],
    "newDiscriminator": "Parent content identity and parent eligibility are orthogonal. An immutable, replayable parent still cannot seed an accepted lineage unless a scoped verifier verdict authorizes that exact parent and the child receipt binds the inherited and changed scopes.",
    "newEvidenceN226": "A rejection registry can prove that listed parents are ineligible, but absence from that denylist is not evidence of scoped parent eligibility. Unknown hashes must fail closed at the promotion boundary."
  },
